d a dynamic value being used with urllib. urllib supports 'file://' schemes, so a dynamic value controlled by a malicious actor may allow them to read arbitrary files. Audit uses of urllib calls to ensure user data cannot control the URLs, or consider using the 'requests' library instead.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://github.com/PyCQA/bandit/blob/b1411bfb43795d3ffd268bef17a839dee954c2b1/bandit/blacklists/calls.py#L163)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/939.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/939.html)\n","text":"Detected a dynamic value being used with urllib. urllib supports 'file://' schemes, so a dynamic value controlled by a malicious actor may allow them to read arbitrary files. Audit uses of urllib calls to ensure user data cannot control the URLs, or consider using the 'requests' library instead."},"helpUri":"https://github.com/PyCQA/bandit/blob/b1411bfb43795d3ffd268bef17a839dee954c2b1/bandit/blacklists/calls.py#L163","id":"Users.ps.semgrep-official.python.lang.security.audit.dynamic-urllib-use-detected","name":"Users.ps.semgrep-official.python.lang.security.audit.dynamic-urllib-use-detected","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-939: Improper Authorization in Handler for Custom URL Scheme","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: Users.ps.semgrep-official.python.lang.security.audit.dynamic-urllib-use-detected"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected the use of eval(). eval() can be dangerous if used to evaluate dynamic content. If this content can be input from outside the program, this may be a code injection vulnerability. Ensure evaluated content is not definable by external sources."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected the use of eval(). eval() can be dangerous if used to evaluate dynamic content. If this content can be input from outside the program, this may be a code injection vulnerability. Ensure evaluated content is not definable by external sources.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://bandit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/blacklists/blacklist_calls.html#b307-eval)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Detected the use of eval(). eval() can be dangerous if used to evaluate dynamic content. If this content can be input from outside the program, this may be a code injection vulnerability. Ensure evaluated content is not definable by external sources."},"helpUri":"https://bandit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/blacklists/blacklist_calls.html#b307-eval","id":"Users.ps.semgrep-official.python.lang.security.audit.eval-detected","name":"Users.ps.semgrep-official.python.lang.security.audit.eval-detected","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-95: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code ('Eval Injection')","LOW CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: Users.ps.semgrep-official.python.lang.security.audit.eval-detected"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected the use of exec(). exec() can be dangerous if used to evaluate dynamic content. If this content can be input from outside the program, this may be a code injection vulnerability. Ensure evaluated content is not definable by external sources."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected the use of exec(). exec() can be dangerous if used to evaluate dynamic content. If this content can be input from outside the program, this may be a code injection vulnerability. Ensure evaluated content is not definable by external sources.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://bandit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/plugins/b102_exec_used.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Detected the use of exec(). exec() can be dangerous if used to evalua